### The LYSO panel as the pixel panel (/tof/czt/...), for the macros that use it (muonic_xray_lyso.mac,
### lyso_decay_only.mac, vis_lyso.mac, panel_xray_gun.mac). Since 2026-11-04 the user's new panel (it replaces the 30 x 30
### one of 6 mm pixels): 20 x 20 pixels of 6.25 x 6.25 x 3 mm LYSO (Lu1.8Y0.2SiO5, 7.2 g/cm3), read out as single pixels,
### 0.08 mm of ESR between them and around the outer ones (pitch 6.33 mm) and a 0.08 mm ESR sheet over them, all in a
### 0.1 mm Al frame on the sides and on top: 126.88 mm wide (6.25 x 20 + 0.08 x 21 + 0.1 x 2) and 3.18 mm thick
### (0.1 + 0.08 + 3). The Al faces the target (coverOnTop); the LYSO's bottom face is open, for the full SiPM readout
### under it (not modelled). ESR (a multilayer polymer reflector) is modelled as G4_MYLAR (PET, 1.40 g/cm3). Its place:
### /tof/czt/position, the centre of the 3 mm pixel layer, set by the macro that executes this one (32.332 cm: the Al
### against the target's bottom face at 32.5 cm, the LYSO at 32.182-32.482 cm). Another detector: a panel_<name>.mac of
### its own with the same commands.

/tof/czt/enable true
/tof/czt/name LYSO
/tof/czt/material LYSO
/tof/czt/pixels 20
/tof/czt/pixelSize 6.25 mm
/tof/czt/pitch 6.33 mm
/tof/czt/thickness 3 mm
/tof/czt/gapMaterial G4_MYLAR
/tof/czt/backThickness 0.08 mm
/tof/czt/frameThickness 0.1 mm
/tof/czt/frameMaterial G4_Al
/tof/czt/coverOnTop true
